{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerLobachevsky","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerSymmetry","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ExponentialGrowthRate","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial"],"declarations":53,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.volume_conjecture_five_two_cLiTwoExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.volume_conjecture_five_two_cLiTwoExt","kind":"theorem","line":1058,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L1058-L1072","doc":"**The bridge at the corpus's own dilogarithm.** The `Li₂` parameter and both\nidentity hypotheses of `volume_conjecture_five_two_wired` are gone.\n\nRead the residue directly off the statement: `[OhtsukiAsymptotic …]` is (A),\n`[FiveTwoTriangulation …]` is (D), and `hζ` is a transcription. Nothing else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.isKummerAtOhtsukiArgs_cLiTwoExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.isKummerAtOhtsukiArgs_cLiTwoExt","kind":"theorem","line":1044,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L1044-L1056","doc":"**Kummer's identity at Ohtsuki's five arguments, for the corpus's own\ndilogarithm.** No hypotheses beyond the shape.\n\n`kummer` states its right-hand side as `log‖z‖ · arg(1−z)`; `IsKummerAt` uses\nthe other factor order, which is what the trailing `ring` is for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.volume_conjecture_five_two_wired","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.volume_conjecture_five_two_wired","kind":"theorem","line":989,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L989-L1024","doc":"**The bridge, wired.** No free identity hypotheses remain.\n\nWhat is assumed, and only this:\n\n* `[OhtsukiAsymptotic …]` — (A), Ohtsuki's Theorem 1.1 at `d = 0`;\n* `[FiveTwoTriangulation (conj (1/y)) vol]` — (D), the corpus's own geometric\n  axiom, at the shape `conj_inv_is_five_two_shape` certifies is admissible;\n* `hbw`, `hone` — that `Li₂` is a dilogarithm (Kummer plus `Li₂(1) ∈ ℝ`),\n  unavoidable while Mathlib has no polylogarithm. `hbw` is now\n  `IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs`: Kummer at **five named points**, not on a half plane.\n  `IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.of_upper_half_plane` builds it from `kummer`'s own\n  `Im z > 0` range plus conjugation symmetry, so nothing here waits on a\n  continuation across the branch cut;\n* `hζ` — Ohtsuki's own **definition** of `ζ`, transcribed.\n\n`hzeta` and `hvol`, which the raw bridge took on faith, are now theorems: the\nfirst is (B) via `two_pi_re_zeta_eq_three_blochWigner`, the second is\n`BlochWigner_lob_conj_inv` applied to the triangulation's `vol_eq_three_D`.\n\nThe residue is exactly the two things this corpus has not proved and does not\nclaim to — Ohtsuki's asymptotic expansion, and the hyperbolic geometry of the\n`5₂` complement's triangulation — plus the statement that a dilogarithm is a\ndilogarithm. Everything between them is derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.volume_conjecture_five_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.volume_conjecture_five_two","kind":"theorem","line":971,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L971-L987","doc":"**The bridge, in its raw form.** Combining (A) with the two identities (B)\nand (D) *as hypotheses*, the volume conjecture holds for `5₂`.\n\nThis is the lemma; `volume_conjecture_five_two_wired` below is the theorem. Both\nare kept: this one is the reusable shape (any knot with an Ohtsuki-type\nexpansion and a `vol = 3·D` triangulation), the wired one is `5₂` with both\nidentities discharged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.growth_rate_eq_two_pi_re_zeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.growth_rate_eq_two_pi_re_zeta","kind":"theorem","line":943,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L943-L969","doc":"**(C).** From the asymptotic form alone, the Kashaev growth rate is\n`2π·Re ζ`.\n\n`log‖e^{Nζ}·N^{3/2}·ω·(1+o(1))‖ = N·Re ζ + (3/2)·log N + log‖ω‖ + o(1)`, and\neverything but the first term dies after dividing by `N`.\n\nNo steepest descent, no geometry — this is the step that makes the shrink pay,\nbecause it shows the volume-conjecture *conclusion* follows from the asymptotic\n*form* by analysis Mathlib already has. Both side conditions it needs — `ω ≠ 0`\nand `⟨5₂⟩_N ≠ 0` — are the two theorems above rather than assumptions.\n\nThe content is entirely generic, and lives in\n`QOU.MathlibExt.tendsto_log_norm_div_of_tendsto_one`: *a sub-exponential factor\ncannot change an exponential growth rate*. Nothing here is about `5₂`, which is\nwhy it is stated once for every knot with such an expansion rather than per\nknot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.kashaev_eventually_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.kashaev_eventually_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":930,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L930-L941","doc":"**A second field that is not a field.** `⟨5₂⟩_N ≠ 0` eventually — because a\nratio tending to `1` is eventually non-zero, and a quotient is non-zero only if\nits numerator is.\n\nWorth isolating: the obvious way to supply this is to assume it, and assuming it\nwould be assuming something about the Kashaev invariant that Ohtsuki's theorem\nalready implies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.omega_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.omega_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":920,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L920-L928","doc":"**The field that is no longer a field.** The previous version of this class\ncarried `omega_ne_zero` as an assumption. It is a theorem: `ω² = i(y−1)/(2y+1)`\nand neither factor vanishes at a root of the cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.OhtsukiAsymptotic.ratio_tendsto_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.OhtsukiAsymptotic.ratio_tendsto_one","kind":"theorem","line":914,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L914-L914","doc":"`⟨5₂⟩_N / (e^{Nζ}·N^{3/2}·ω) → 1`. This is the only analytic content.\n\n`N^{3/2}` is written as a *real* power cast into `ℂ`, not as `Complex.cpow`.\nThat is the faithful reading — Ohtsuki's `N^{3/2}` is a positive real, and\n`cpow` would drag in a branch choice he does not make — and it is also what\nlets `Real.log_rpow` reach it in the proof of (C). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.OhtsukiAsymptotic.omega_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.OhtsukiAsymptotic.omega_sq","kind":"theorem","line":907,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L907-L907","doc":"`ω` is Ohtsuki's explicit prefactor `e^{iπ/4}·((y−1)/(2y+1))^{1/2}`,\nstated through its square so that no branch has to be chosen — and so that\n`ω ≠ 0` becomes derivable rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.OhtsukiAsymptotic.shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.OhtsukiAsymptotic.shape","kind":"theorem","line":903,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L903-L903","doc":"`y` is the root of `(y−1)³ = y` in the upper half plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.OhtsukiAsymptotic.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.OhtsukiAsymptotic.mk","kind":"ctor","line":901,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L901-L901","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.OhtsukiAsymptotic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.OhtsukiAsymptotic","kind":"class","line":897,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L897-L918","doc":"**(A), the shrunk axiom** — the `d = 0` truncation of Ohtsuki's Theorem 1.1.\n\nDeliberately carries no instance (AGENTS.md §3b-tax): the honest representation\nof an input this corpus has not proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.conj_inv_is_five_two_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.conj_inv_is_five_two_shape","kind":"theorem","line":882,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L882-L889","doc":"**The `5₂` shape the corpus triangulates is admissible for Ohtsuki's root.**\nBoth `FiveTwoTriangulation` side conditions hold at `conj (1/y₀)`, so asking for\nthat instance asks only for the *geometric* content (`vol = 3·D`), never for an\nunchecked algebraic claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.conj_inv_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.conj_inv_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":872,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L872-L880","doc":"…and it is in the **upper** half plane, which the bare inversion is not:\n`Im (1/y) = −Im y/|y|² < 0`, and conjugating flips it back. This is exactly why\nthe corpus's `y₊` is the conjugate rather than the reciprocal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.saddle_root_conj_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.saddle_root_conj_inv","kind":"theorem","line":860,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L860-L870","doc":"`conj (1/y₀)` is a root of the corpus's `5₂` **saddle** cubic. The\nconjugation is free because that cubic has real (indeed integer) coefficients;\nthe inversion is `inv_root_of_ohtsuki_cubic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.two_pi_re_zeta_eq_three_blochWigner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.two_pi_re_zeta_eq_three_blochWigner","kind":"theorem","line":826,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L826-L840","doc":"**(B), in the form the bridge consumes.** `2π·Re ζ = 3·D(y₀)` when `ζ` is\nOhtsuki's `ζ` — i.e. the `hzeta` hypothesis of `volume_conjecture_five_two`,\ndischarged.\n\n`hζ` is not an extra assumption about the world: it is the *definition* of `ζ`\nin Ohtsuki's Theorem 1.1, transcribed. What used to be an unproved identity\nbetween two independently-named quantities is now a substitution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.two_pi_mul_re_of_div_two_pi_I","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.two_pi_mul_re_of_div_two_pi_I","kind":"theorem","line":809,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L809-L824","doc":"`2π·Re (S/(2π√−1)) = Im S`. Pure arithmetic; isolated because it is the only\nplace the `√−1` in Ohtsuki's normalisation is used, and getting its sign wrong\nwould flip `Vol` against the Chern–Simons invariant without any other symptom.\n\nProof shape: clear the denominator to `ζ·2π√−1 = S` and read off imaginary\nparts, rather than expanding `Complex.div_re`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.ohtsuki_sum_im_eq_three_blochWigner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.ohtsuki_sum_im_eq_three_blochWigner","kind":"theorem","line":616,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L616-L799","doc":"**(B) — PROVED.**\n\n`Im` of Ohtsuki's five-term dilogarithm sum is `3·D(y₀)`, with no geometry and\nno asymptotics.\n\n## What the hypotheses are, and why they are not the theorem in disguise\n\nMathlib has no polylogarithm, so `Li₂` is a parameter. It is constrained by\nexactly two facts, both of which the corpus proves for its **own** dilogarithm\n`QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt`:\n\n* `hbw` is **Kummer's identity**, `D(z) = Im Li₂(z) + arg(1−z)·log‖z‖` — the\n  statement that the Λ-built `BlochWigner_lob` and the `Li₂`-built Bloch–Wigner\n  function are the same function — asserted at the **five points** this proof\n  applies it to and nowhere else (`IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs`, above).\n  `QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.kummer` proves it sorry-free for `Im z > 0`, which\n  covers two of the five; the other three are `1/y₀`, `1/x₀` and `1/(x₀y₀)`, in\n  the *lower* half plane, and `IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.of_upper_half_plane`\n  reaches them from the upper ones given only that `Li₂` commutes with\n  conjugation off the real axis. So no continuation across the cut is needed.\n* `hone` is `Im Li₂(1) = 0`, i.e. `Li₂(1) = π²/6` is real. It is stated\n  separately because `hbw` is deliberately *not* assumed at `z = 1`, where\n  `arg(1 − z) = arg 0` and the identity holds only through Lean's `arg 0 = 0`\n  convention.\n\nNeither hypothesis mentions `5₂`, the cubic, or a volume.\n\n## ⚠ The hypothesis this replaces was FALSE\n\nUntil this proof was written the statement also carried\n\n```\nhinv : ∀ z ≠ 0, Im Li₂(z) + Im Li₂(1/z) = −2·arg(1−z)·log‖z‖\n```\n\nadvertised as \"the inversion formula\". **It is not the inversion formula and it\nis not true.** Euler's inversion `Li₂(z) + Li₂(1/z) = −π²/6 − ½log(−z)²` has\nimaginary part `−log‖z‖·arg(−z)`, and `arg(−z) ≠ 2·arg(1−z)`. Measured against\n`mpmath` at 40 digits, the discharged form is off by `−2.97e-1` at `y₀`,\n`−9.17e-2` at `x₀` and `−7.25e-3` at `x₀y₀` — not a branch ambiguity, a wrong\nidentity. Worse, it is inconsistent with `hbw`, which already determines\n`Im Li₂` completely; so the old statement was a `sorry` guarding a hypothesis\nset no dilogarithm satisfies. It is gone, and nothing replaced it: the correct\ninversion is *derivable* here from `hbw` plus `D(1/z) = −D(z)`, so the theorem\nnow needs one identity where it claimed to need two.\n\n**The check that failure teaches: are the surviving hypotheses satisfiable?**\nA theorem whose hypotheses no object satisfies is vacuous, and that is exactly\nwhat the old one was. `hbw` and `hone` are independent — `hbw` is asserted only\nat the five non-unit arguments, `hone` only at `z = 1` — and the\nprincipal-branch `Li₂` satisfies both: `Im Li₂(1) = Im(π²/6) = 0`, and `hbw` was\nchecked at 40 digits at fourteen random points in **both** half planes (worst\ndeviation `7.8e-41`) as well as at all five arguments this proof actually uses.\nAny new hypothesis added here should get the same treatment before it is\ntrusted — as the conjugation hypothesis of `of_upper_half_plane` was, where the\ncheck caught that the *unrestricted* form is unsatisfiable.\n\n## The proof, in one line per term\n\nApply `hbw` at each of the five non-unit arguments, then use\n`BlochWigner_lob_inv` (`D(1/z) = −D(z)`) and `blochWigner_xOf_eq`\n(`D(x₀) = D(y₀)`). The `D` terms give\n\n```\nD(−w) − D(−w) + D(y) + D(y) + D(x₀) = 3·D(y)\n```\n\n— note `D(x₀y₀)` cancels against itself between the first two terms, so the\n`D(x₀y₀) = D(y₀)/2` that an earlier version of this docstring listed as\nrequired is **not needed**. (It is true — measured to 50 digits — but it is not\non the path.)\n\nThe correction terms are all of the form `(integer · arg w) · (integer · log‖w‖)`\nbecause of the `w`-power identities above, and the integers cancel:\n\n```\narg:   1 − 1/(x₀y₀) contributes +1 ,  1 − y contributes −3 ,\n       1 − 1/y = x₀ contributes +6 ,  1 − 1/x₀     contributes −2      →  0\n```\n\nThe `arg(2 − y₀)` terms — the only ones that are *not* multiples of `arg w` —\ncancel in pairs between `Li₂(x₀y₀)` and `Li₂(1/(x₀y₀))` before any of that.\n\n## Errors the typechecker caught, recorded for the next reader\n\n* `Complex.arg_mul` needs `arg a + arg b ∈ Ioc (−π) π`, and for `(2−y)/(1−y)`\n  the sum is `arg(2−y) + (−arg w)`, in `(−π/2, π)` — it is *not* symmetric about\n  `0`, so the two bounds have genuinely different proofs.\n* `arg((1−y)²) = 2·arg(1−y)` is only true because `2·arg w ∈ (−π, 0)`; the naive\n  `arg_pow` is a `Real.Angle` statement and does not give it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.of_upper_half_plane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.of_upper_half_plane","kind":"theorem","line":601,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L601-L614","doc":"**What the `5₂` bridge really needs of a dilogarithm.** Kummer's identity on\nthe *upper* half plane — which `QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.kummer` proves — together\nwith conjugation symmetry off the real axis.\n\nThis retires \"extend `kummer` across the real axis by Schwarz reflection\" as the\nblocker: it is sufficient to know that `Li₂` commutes with conjugation, which is\na statement about `Li₂`'s own series/integral representation and needs no\ncontinuation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.isKummerAt_of_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.isKummerAt_of_upper","kind":"theorem","line":585,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L585-L599","doc":"**Kummer on the upper half plane, plus conjugation symmetry, gives Kummer\noff the real axis.**\n\nThis is *not* an analytic continuation: `hupper` is only ever evaluated where it\nalready holds, and the lower half plane is reached by the algebraic identity\nabove. `hconj` is restricted to `w.im ≠ 0` because the unrestricted form is\nfalse on the cut (see the section docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.isKummerAt_of_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.isKummerAt_of_conj","kind":"theorem","line":562,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L562-L583","doc":"**Kummer transports across the real axis by conjugation.**\n\nEvery ingredient of the identity is odd under `z ↦ z̄` in the same way:\n`D(z̄) = −D(z)` (`BlochWigner_lob_conj`), `Im Li₂(z̄) = −Im Li₂(z)` (the\nhypothesis), `arg(1 − z̄) = −arg(1 − z)` (`arg_conj_of_im_ne_zero`, and\n`1 − z` is off the axis exactly when `z` is), and `‖z̄‖ = ‖z‖`. So the identity\nat `z̄` is `(−1)×` the identity at `z`, and `linear_combination -h` is the\nwhole proof.\n\nThe hypothesis is one equation at one point, not a functional equation: this is\nSchwarz reflection reduced to what the bridge actually needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.of_forall","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.of_forall","kind":"theorem","line":547,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L547-L560","doc":"**The old half-plane hypothesis still discharges the new one.** Anything\nthat could supply `∀ z, z.im ≠ 0 → …` to this bridge is unaffected by the\nweakening. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.xOf_mul_self_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.xOf_mul_self_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":540,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L540-L545","doc":"`x₀y₀ = y₀ − 1` is off the real axis at any Ohtsuki shape — the shift is\nreal, so it moves nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.xOf_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.xOf_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":534,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L534-L538","doc":"`x₀ = 1 − 1/y` is off the real axis whenever `y` is: `Im x₀ = −Im (1/y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.at_inv_x","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.at_inv_x","kind":"theorem","line":532,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L532-L532","doc":"at `1/x₀` — lower half plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.at_inv_y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.at_inv_y","kind":"theorem","line":530,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L530-L530","doc":"at `1/y₀` — lower half plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.at_y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.at_y","kind":"theorem","line":528,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L528-L528","doc":"at `y₀` — upper half plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.at_inv_xy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.at_inv_xy","kind":"theorem","line":526,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L526-L526","doc":"at `1/(x₀y₀)` — lower half plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.at_xy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.at_xy","kind":"theorem","line":524,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L524-L524","doc":"at `x₀y₀ = y₀ − 1` — upper half plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs.mk","kind":"ctor","line":522,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L522-L522","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs","kind":"structure","line":516,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L516-L532","doc":"**The five points.** Exactly the Kummer instances\n`ohtsuki_sum_im_eq_three_blochWigner` consumes, one per non-unit argument of\n`ohtsukiSum`.\n\n`z = 1` is deliberately absent: it is handled by the separate `hone`, because\nthere the identity holds only through Lean's `arg 0 = 0` convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsKummerAt","kind":"def","line":507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L507-L514","doc":"**Kummer's identity at one point**: the Λ-built `BlochWigner_lob` and the\n`Li₂`-built Bloch–Wigner function agree at `z`.\n\nSplit out of the old `∀`-hypothesis so the bridge can name the points it uses.\nNot a convenience abbreviation — `IsKummerAtOhtsukiArgs` is the honest statement\nof everything the `5₂` bridge assumes about a dilogarithm away from `z = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.one_sub_re_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.one_sub_re_pos","kind":"theorem","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L433-L465","doc":"**`Re(1 − y) > 0` at every non-real root of Ohtsuki's cubic.**\n\nEquivalently `Re y < 1` — measured, `Re y₀ = 0.3376…`. This pins `w = 1 − y` to\nthe fourth quadrant (together with `Im w = −Im y < 0`), hence\n`arg w ∈ (−π/2, 0)`, which is what every `arg` computation below rests on.\n\nThe hypothesis is `y.im ≠ 0`, not `0 < y.im`: the statement is about the\nconjugate *pair*, and using less than is available keeps the reason visible —\nthe real root `y = 2.3247…` genuinely has `Re y > 1`, so some hypothesis\nexcluding it is unavoidable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.one_sub_one_div_xOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.one_sub_one_div_xOf","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L400-L409","doc":"`1 − 1/x₀ = 1/w`, and — a small surprise — **the cubic is not needed**.\n\n`x₀ = 1 − 1/y` is the order-3 Möbius map, so `1 − 1/x₀` is that map applied\ntwice, which the 3-cycle already evaluates: it is `one_sub_inv_mobius` in\n`BlochWignerSymmetry.lean`, proved there for every `y ∉ {0,1}`. An earlier draft\nrouted this through `w³ = w − 1` and needed the root; that was strictly more\nthan the fact costs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.xOf_eq_one_div_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.xOf_eq_one_div_sq","kind":"theorem","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L386-L398","doc":"`x₀ = 1/w²`. This is the cubic doing real work: `x₀ = (y−1)/y` and `y =\n(y−1)³`, so the `(y−1)` cancels down to `(y−1)^{-2}`.\n\nThe `linear_combination` certificate is `+h`, not `−h`: `field_simp` normalises\nthe cleared equation with the *opposite* orientation to the one this file's\nother certificates use, and the typechecker rejects the sign immediately. Worth\nrecording only because the same wrong guess costs a compile every time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.xOf_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.xOf_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L379-L384","doc":"`x₀·y₀ = y₀ − 1 = −w`. No cubic needed — this is just `(1 − 1/y)·y`.\n\nWorth stating on its own: Ohtsuki writes `Li₂(x₀y₀)`, and the product is a\n*translate* of `y₀`, not a new transcendental. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.eq_neg_one_sub_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.eq_neg_one_sub_cube","kind":"theorem","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L373-L377","doc":"`y = −w³`. The volume-carrying consequence: `‖y‖ = ‖w‖³`, so `log‖y‖` is\n*three* times `log‖w‖` — the `3` in `3·D(y₀)` and the `3` in the coefficient\nbookkeeping are the same `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.cubic_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.cubic_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L364-L371","doc":"The cubic recentred at `w = 1 − y`: `w³ − w + 1 = 0`, i.e. `w³ = w − 1`.\n\nNote this is the *plastic-number* cubic with a sign: `u³ = u + 1` for `u = y−1`.\nThe `5₂` shape field is ℚ(`u`), the complex cubic field of discriminant `−23` —\nthe smallest `|disc|` there is, which is why `Vol(5₂)` is the smallest volume in\nthe Zagier tables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.ohtsukiSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.ohtsukiSum","kind":"def","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L339-L345","doc":"Ohtsuki's potential function `V(x,y)`, evaluated along `x = x₀(y)`.\n`Li₂` is written abstractly: this file does not construct a complex\npolylogarithm, it takes one as a parameter, so the statement is independent of\nwhichever `Li₂` the corpus or Mathlib eventually supplies. The final `Li₂ 1`\nterm is `π²/6`; it is real, so it drops out of the imaginary part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.kappaOne_numerator_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.kappaOne_numerator_identity","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L322-L331","doc":"The two printed forms of `κ₁ − 1` agree, with denominators cleared. The\ncertificate is exact: `A·12696 − B·(2y+1)³ = −4(3300y² + 7854y + 13337)·cubic`.\n\nThis is corroboration only — `κ₁` plays no part in the volume conjecture, which\nneeds the leading term alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.two_I_mul_ohtsukiOmegaSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.two_I_mul_ohtsukiOmegaSq","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L298-L313","doc":"The quantity Ohtsuki–Takata's Theorem 1.1 identifies (up to sign) with the\ntwisted Reidemeister torsion. Their statement is about `ω²(D)`, a modification\nof the Hessian of the potential function; here we record only the elementary\nhalf — that Ohtsuki's own `ω` makes `2√−1·ω²` a rational function of `y₀`.\n\nMeasured: `−2(y₀−1)/(2y₀+1) = 0.2344867660… − √−1·0.8286683659…`, matching the\nmodulus of Ohtsuki–Takata's printed `τ(5₂)` (their value is the negated\nconjugate, the usual conjugate-geometric-solution convention).\n\nNo hypothesis is needed: when `2y + 1 = 0` both sides are division by zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.ohtsukiOmegaSq_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.ohtsukiOmegaSq_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L289-L296","doc":"**The shrink.** Ohtsuki's prefactor is non-zero — and this is now a\nconsequence of the cubic rather than a hypothesis carried by the axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.ohtsukiOmegaSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.ohtsukiOmegaSq","kind":"def","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L285-L287","doc":"`ω² = i·(y−1)/(2y+1)`, Ohtsuki's prefactor squared. Rational in `y` up to\nthe factor `i`; no square root, no dilogarithm, nothing transcendental. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.xOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.xOf","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L278-L279","doc":"The auxiliary shape `x₀ = 1 − 1/y₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.inv_root_of_ohtsuki_cubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.inv_root_of_ohtsuki_cubic","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L268-L276","doc":"Ohtsuki's cubic is the reciprocal of the corpus's `fiveTwoSaddleCubic`.\nIf `y ≠ 0` satisfies `y³ − 3y² + 2y − 1 = 0` then `w = 1/y` satisfies\n`w³ − 2w² + 3w − 1 = 0`. This is the algebraic half of the reconciliation\nbetween the two cubics; the conjugation half is `D(z̄) = −D(z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.exists_isOhtsukiShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.exists_isOhtsukiShape","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L208-L266","doc":"**`IsOhtsukiShape` is inhabited.** Bean `qou-6x46`.\n\nEvery theorem in this file takes `IsOhtsukiShape y` as a hypothesis, directly or\nas the `shape` field of `OhtsukiAsymptotic`, and until this lemma **nothing in\nthe corpus showed that hypothesis was satisfiable** — `exact?` could not close\n`∃ y, IsOhtsukiShape y` on 2026-08-31. A conditional theorem whose condition is\nnot known to be met is a different and weaker object than one conditional on a\npublished result, and the corpus's vacuity audits exist to keep the two apart.\n\n**Constructed, not counted.** No root-multiset or discriminant machinery:\n\n1. the intermediate value theorem gives the real root `t ∈ [2.3, 2.4]`, since\n   `p(2.3) = −0.103 < 0 < 0.344 = p(2.4)`;\n2. dividing out `(y − t)` leaves `y² + (t−3)y + (t²−3t+2)`, whose discriminant is\n   `−(3t² − 6t − 1)` — and `3t² − 6t − 1 > 0` for `t ≥ 2.3`, which is exactly why\n   the bracket is taken there rather than at the obvious `[2,3]`: at `t = 2`\n   the quantity is `−1`, so the coarse bracket does not decide the sign;\n3. its two roots are then written down, and the one with `+√d` has `Im > 0`.\n\nThe division in step 2 is legitimate only modulo the cubic — the cofactor's\nconstant term is `1/t`, and `t² − 3t + 2 = 1/t` *is* `p(t) = 0` rearranged, so\nthe whole identity is one `linear_combination` against `ht`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsOhtsukiShape.two_mul_add_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsOhtsukiShape.two_mul_add_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L204-L206","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsOhtsukiShape.ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsOhtsukiShape.ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L201-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsOhtsukiShape.ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsOhtsukiShape.ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L198-L199","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.cubic_two_mul_add_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.cubic_two_mul_add_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L189-L196","doc":"`−1/2` is not a root: it gives `−23/8 = 0`. Hence the denominator of\nOhtsuki's prefactor never vanishes — from the cubic, not from `Im y > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.cubic_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.cubic_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L185-L187","doc":"`1` is not a root: it gives `1 − 3 + 2 − 1 = −1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.cubic_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.cubic_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L181-L183","doc":"`0` is not a root: it gives `−1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsOhtsukiShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.IsOhtsukiShape","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.lean#L176-L179","doc":"Ohtsuki's shape: a root of `(y − 1)³ = y`, i.e. of `y³ − 3y² + 2y − 1`,\nwith positive imaginary part. Stated as a predicate rather than constructed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}